From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:23:21 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 27/72] deepseek: carry native image requests through shared
 serving

Port the family codecs, preprocessing, tower and aligner into the current
native engine. Validate image roles and all-rank boot settings before
planning buffers, retain request owners through terminal events, and keep
text-only multi-segment prefill settings after image preparation.

Exercise image admission, exact bias widening, ownership, codec boundaries
and retained-request map churn with host fixtures. Register the vision
launches with the shared kernel contract; device and checkpoint gates
remain unqualified.

The WebP codec port includes QP's recipe boundary fixes from fa8853a0cc.
